ry_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Sentence Stress - Disbelief or Surprise"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use sentence stress on some words in a sentence. These are content words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Content words are the key (important) words of a sentence.  You place emphasis on these words."}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you want to express surprise or disbelief, the sound at the end of the sentence changes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use rising intonation to tell the listener that you are surprised by what they just heard."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class= \"italic\">Example: Wow, that's amazing!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use falling intonation to express sarcasm or disbelief."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class= \"italic\">Example: I don't believe that!</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "big kid "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to act in a child-like way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My boyfriend was acting like a big kid."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when people talk about dating."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flock "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of birds or animals "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:The flock of geese was moving towards us. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hiss "}, {"type": "definition", "content":